+ * target scan and a changelog.  It exists so that a consumer holding a FID --
+ * a changelog reader, above all -- fills a record the same way the walk does,
+ * the layout included, rather than from an fstat() of its own that answers six
+ * predicates out of eighty.  The default demand mask is the walk's, so the
+ * three fields that cost an ioctl or an open per object -- LLAPI_SCAN_HSM,
+ * LLAPI_SCAN_PROJID and LLAPI_SCAN_MDT_INDEX -- arrive only when lfsp_want
+ * names them.
+ *
+ * The FID is resolved to a pathname and the record gathered there, which is
+ * why the caller needs whatever llapi_fid2path_at() needs:
+ * CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH, unless llite.*.user_fid2path is set.  An object that
+ * has been unlinked since the caller learned of it no longer resolves and is
+ * reported as -ENOENT; for a consumer asking what is true now, that is the
+ * answer rather than an error to work around.
+ *
+ * The record is filled from the live object and nothing in it is carried in
+ * from the caller.  A consumer merging this into a record it already holds
+ * decides for itself which fields it lets this one supply -- which is how
+ * lfs find --changelog --resolve uses it, filling only what the stream
+ * lacks.
